From a2b3952ebee6fe2dbc030c9164e1f6c0125fd423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 17:35:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CRITICAL FIX: Anti-ban interval enforcement - 3 bugs fixed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. SELF-LOCK LOOP BUG: Chip lock (nextSendAt+120s) was being detected
   by the same process's nextSendAt check, causing infinite loop of
   claim→lock→reject→release→claim. Fix: track lock timestamp and
   skip check if nextSendAt matches our own lock.

2. CLUSTER MICRO-PAUSE EXCEPTION: Micro-pauses allowed gaps as short
   as 30s (or 2-7s with race conditions) between messages from the
   same chip, despite messageIntervalMin=59s. Fix: messageIntervalMin
   is now the absolute minimum for ALL delay types, no exceptions.
   ABSOLUTE_MIN_INTERVAL raised from 30s to 60s.

3. RELEASE MESSAGE CLEARING LEGITIMATE LOCKS: releaseMessageAndChipLock
   was clearing ANY nextSendAt within 2 minutes, including legitimate
   intervals set by successful sends. Fix: only clear nextSendAt if it
   matches our temporary lock timestamp (±2s tolerance).

4. IN-MEMORY SEND GUARD: Added per-chip last-send timestamp cache as
   a last-resort protection against race conditions where concurrent
   cron ticks both select the same chip.
---
